According to Article 21, freedom of movement in Ghana includes:

- The right to move freely within Ghana;
- The right to leave Ghana;
- The right to enter Ghana; and
- Immunity from expulsion from Ghana.

These rights are explicitly stated under clause (1)(g) of Article 21 (Chapter 5, Article 21, p.43).

